WEBVTT

00:00:03.480 --> 00:00:11.180
Molly, I need your special talent for handling special matters.

00:00:12.460 --> 00:00:13.800
Like what special matters?

00:00:15.060 --> 00:00:16.880
Well, I have a scheduling problem.

00:00:17.480 --> 00:00:18.040
Yes?

00:00:18.760 --> 00:00:21.700
I have three tonsillectomies set for Friday with Dr. Earl.

00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:22.700
Yes?

00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:26.780
I need to fit a fourth operation into his schedule.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:30.020
And ... I know you can do it.

00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:31.500
Who's the patient?

00:00:32.080 --> 00:00:33.020
Carl Herrera.

00:00:33.260 --> 00:00:34.820
The boy has infected tonsils,

00:00:34.820 --> 00:00:36.640
and we should remove them as soon as possible.

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:40.860
But it's not going to be easy.

00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:45.900
I know you'll be able to take care of it.

00:00:47.620 --> 00:00:49.180
Well, Mrs. Herrera,

00:00:49.480 --> 00:00:52.660
Carl will be perfectly fine after we remove his tonsils.

00:00:53.020 --> 00:00:55.440
Thank you for your reassurance, Dr. Stewart.

00:00:55.780 --> 00:00:58.260
He's had so many colds and sore throats recently.

00:00:58.710 --> 00:01:01.160
Well, it's a very easy operation, Carl.

00:01:01.180 --> 00:01:02.420
You won't feel a thing.

00:01:02.540 --> 00:01:04.040
But when do they do it?

00:01:04.920 --> 00:01:05.840
This Friday.

00:01:06.680 --> 00:01:08.500
But Saturday's my birthday.

00:01:09.840 --> 00:01:14.540
Well, we could reschedule the operation, Mrs. Herrera,

00:01:14.740 --> 00:01:17.340
but I don't want to put it off too long.

00:01:17.340 --> 00:01:19.560
No, I think it's important to do it now.

00:01:20.260 --> 00:01:22.310
We can have a birthday party for you, Carl,

00:01:22.310 --> 00:01:23.520
When you come out of the hospital.

00:01:23.720 --> 00:01:25.780
But it won't be on my birthday.

00:01:26.180 --> 00:01:29.040
But your health is more important, Carl. Believe me.

00:01:29.480 --> 00:01:31.680
I don't want my tonsils out.

00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:37.140
Nurse Baker, would you come in, please?

00:01:41.720 --> 00:01:47.080
Hello, Mrs. Herrera. Hi, Carl, how are you doing?

00:01:47.460 --> 00:01:49.660
I don't want my tonsils out.

00:01:50.860 --> 00:01:52.240
Come with me, Carl.

00:01:52.280 --> 00:01:53.860
You and I will talk this over.

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:00.960
She has a special way with kids.

00:02:01.480 --> 00:02:02.520
She sure does.

00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:08.960
Yes.

00:02:09.490 --> 00:02:11.810
OK. Do you want to get better?

00:02:12.180 --> 00:02:12.820
Yes.

00:02:13.130 --> 00:02:15.320
OK. We want you to get better, too.

00:02:15.740 --> 00:02:17.320
You'll have your tonsils out tomorrow,

00:02:17.760 --> 00:02:19.680
and you won't get so many colds anymore.

00:02:20.180 --> 00:02:22.320
But if I have my tonsils out tomorrow,

00:02:22.680 --> 00:02:25.000
I'll miss my birthday party on Saturday.

00:02:25.610 --> 00:02:26.560
I know.

00:02:26.980 --> 00:02:28.380
It's a problem, isn't it?

00:02:29.360 --> 00:02:31.220
Let me try to work something out.

00:02:32.420 --> 00:02:33.160
What?

00:02:34.080 --> 00:02:35.680
I have to think about it.

00:02:36.020 --> 00:02:37.520
You're fooling me.

00:02:37.740 --> 00:02:39.300
Oh, I'm not, Carl.

00:02:39.880 --> 00:02:41.660
Give me a chance to think about it,

00:02:41.660 --> 00:02:43.640
and I'll come up with something.

00:02:44.100 --> 00:02:44.840
A surprise?

00:02:45.260 --> 00:02:45.740
Maybe.

00:02:46.200 --> 00:02:48.170
But you just put on your pajamas and robe,

00:02:48.170 --> 00:02:49.720
and I'll think of a surprise.

00:02:50.800 --> 00:02:51.880
Will it hurt?

00:02:52.080 --> 00:02:52.540
No.

00:02:52.880 --> 00:02:54.260
There are other boys and girls here,

00:02:54.260 --> 00:02:55.680
and they're having their tonsils out.

00:02:55.940 --> 00:02:56.520
You'll meet them.

00:02:56.800 --> 00:02:58.240
I don't want to.

00:03:01.700 --> 00:03:03.240
Everything will be just fine.
